1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,880
 Welcome to this lesson on payment plans and features.

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:07,840
 In this session, we'll walk through the different tiers available and how they align

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,840
 with common development needs.

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:15,440
 Choosing the right plan isn't about unlocking features, but about matching usage patterns.

5
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:18,960
 Each tier is designed for a different type of developer or team.

6
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:23,040
 We'll cover who each plan is for, what you get, and the trade-offs to consider.

7
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:26,720
 This will help you make a confident decision as your projects grow.

8
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:30,080
 By the end, you should know exactly what you fit.

9
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:34,480
 Antigravity offers four tiers designed to support different workflows.

10
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:38,800
 The individual plan is aimed at students and hobbyists getting started.

11
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:44,560
 The developer, or pro-plan, supports developers who code daily and need higher limits.

12
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:50,320
 The team plan is built for collaborative environments where multiple developers work together.

13
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:54,800
 Finally, the organization plan is intended for enterprise scale deployment.

14
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:00,640
 Each tier focuses on scale, access, and usage needs rather than feature differences.

15
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:04,240
 This structure makes it easier to upgrade as your work evolves.

16
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:08,640
 The individual plan is a great way to start without financial commitment.

17
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:14,160
 Its ideal for students, hobbyists, and developers exploring the platform during the preview phase.

18
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:20,080
 You get full access to core AI features including smart code suggestions and agent-based tasks.

19
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:26,000
 Browser automation capabilities are also included. The main limitation is weekly usage quotas,

20
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,560
 which cap how much you can use the tool.

21
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:32,320
 This makes the plan best suited for learning and smaller projects.

22
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:35,760
 It's a low-risk way to see how antigravity fits your workflow.

23
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:40,640
 The developer or pro-plan is designed for professionals who use antigravity every day.

24
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:45,600
 It supports longer coding sessions and larger projects without frequent interruptions.

25
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:49,360
 Usage limits are much higher and quarters refresh faster.

26
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:53,280
 You also get priority access and smoother performance overall.

27
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:57,680
 This plan is best for developers who rely on the tool throughout their workday.

28
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:02,720
 One important note is that it requires a separate Google AI Pro or Ultra subscription.

29
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:06,160
 If consistency and speed matter, this tier is a strong feat.

30
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:10,400
 If the team plan focuses on collaboration across multiple developers,

31
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:14,880
 it allows shared access so teams can work together seamlessly.

32
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:20,480
 Usage limits are expanded to support team-level workloads rather than individual use.

33
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:24,880
 Admin controls give workspace administrators centralized oversight.

34
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:28,400
 This makes it easier to manage access usage and governance.

35
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:32,800
 The plan is built specifically for organizations using Google workspace.

36
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:38,080
 It's a good choice for startups and development teams working on shared projects.

37
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:41,840
 The organization plan is an upcoming enterprise focused tier.

38
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:47,200
 It's designed for large companies deploying antigravity across entire development organizations.

39
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:51,920
 This plan emphasizes advanced security, compliance, and data governance.

40
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:56,480
 Custom support options include dedicated channels and personalized onboarding.

41
00:02:56,480 --> 00:03:01,760
 It also supports large numbers of developers with centralized billing and admin management.

42
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:06,240
 This tier is best suited for enterprise environments with strict requirements.

43
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:09,680
 More details will become available as these plan launches.

44
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:12,160
 Getting started with antigravity is straightforward.

45
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:18,240
 You can begin with the free individual plan during the preview phase and explore all core features.

46
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:21,680
 As your needs grow, upgrading to another tier is seamless.

47
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:26,560
 The most important factor is aligning your plan with how often you work and that was scale.

48
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:29,680
 Team size and project complexity should guide your decision.

49
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,640
 Feature access remains consistent across tiers.

50
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:36,960
 Choose the plan that matches your workflow today and adjust as you grow.

51
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,480
 See you in the next lesson.

